Well, I don't know ... If I had magic resistance or reflection I would
be all for that gnome being able to wish up a wand of death :-)

Seriously, how hard would it be to implement monster wishing? You
could just make a table of useful things a monster might want and then
randomly pick an item from it. If you wanted to be fancy, you could
even try to assess the monster's situation and have it wish for
something appropriate.

Let's see now:
1. Dragon scale mail, picked according to what resistance the monster
thinks it needs (for monsters able to wear armor of course)
2. Wand of death
3. Artifact? (even if this is allowed, monsters probably shouldn't be
able to wish for quest artifacts)
4. Amulet of life saving
5. Cockatrice corpse (for monsters with gloves and able to use
weapons)
6. Blessed figurine of an archon.  Just kidding, I know monsters can't
use figurines.  But maybe they should be able to.

What else?  What would you wish for if you were a monster?

Hmmm, this would be a patch that nobody would want to install.

